// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
// Unit test of the Metal tessellation path (renderer_metal/mtl_tessellation, mtl_shader's
// tessellation variants and PsoCache::GetTessellationPipeline, plan P4.4): the vertex shader as a
// compute kernel, the control shader as a compute kernel, the evaluation shader as a
// post-tessellation vertex function, through the same compile, pipeline and encode functions the
// rasterizer uses.
//   (a) GPU correctness: GLSL shaders (glslang, embedded below) draw two quad patches and two
//       triangle patches with known tessellation factors (4) into two RGBA32F targets, which are
//       read back: coverage of the patch areas and nothing outside, the interpolated attribute
//       (bilinear / barycentric of the control points' colours), the patch constant, the patch
//       number (gl_PrimitiveID), the vertex indices the vertex shader saw (first vertex, uint16
//       and uint32 indices, index buffer offset, base vertex) and the instance index;
//   (b) winding: with the domain coordinates mapped straight to clip space, which of the
//       VertexOrderCw/Ccw shaders is culled for the front face CW or CCW (the Vulkan semantics:
//       Cw triangles are clockwise on screen, quads and triangles);
//   (c) the game's shaders: every tessellated pipeline key of the shader cache of a game run
//       (the Vulkan one and the Metal backend's) compiles in its variants (vertex kernels for
//       the three index types, control kernel, evaluation function) and builds as a pipeline.
// MTL_DEBUG_LAYER is switched on (an error asserts) unless the environment sets it. Needs a Metal
// device, no window or game.
//
//   mtl-tessellation-test [<shader cache dir>...]
//
// Directories default to ~/Games/Bloodborne/bench/testuser/cache/CUSA03173 and CUSA03173-metal
// (read only; a directory whose name ends in "-metal" holds the Metal backend's serialized
// pipeline part, the other one Vulkan's).
